@startuml state-request-locale
!include include/style.iuml
title Request locale lifecycle
hide empty description

[*] --> Resolving : request or WebSocket\nconnection received

state Resolving : sources asked in configured order
state Active {
  state Resolved : a source matched\na supported locale
  state Defaulted : no source matched,\ndefault locale used
  state Overridden : changed by set_locale(),\nfor example from the user's profile
  Resolved --> Overridden : set_locale()
  Defaulted --> Overridden : set_locale()
  Overridden --> Overridden : set_locale()
}
Resolving --> Resolved
Resolving --> Defaulted
Active --> Committed : response start sent\n(Content-Language written)
state Committed : translations still follow set_locale()\nbut headers can no longer change
Committed --> Closed : response body sent and\nbackground tasks finished
Closed --> [*] : context variable reset

note right of Active
  use_locale() shadows the request locale
  inside a block and restores it on exit.
  It never changes Content-Language.
end note
@enduml
